### 📚 Description

nitro v3 no longer parses runtime config overrides with `destr`, which. means that numbers/booleans/etc. are all just strings.

at the same time, there's long been a desire to have a hook (https://github.com/nuxt/nuxt/issues/15366) or something to define runtime config programmatically, and to add better typing than currently is supported with the type inference of the default value of runtime config.

rather than bringing back `destr` (which had some unfortunate consequences, such as 'number-looking' strings being coerced to _numbers_), this PR treats each value in `runtimeConfig` as an inferred schema, where the value is the default and its type is the type an env override is converted to.

for when that isn't enough, any value can be a [Standard Schema](https://standardschema.dev) that also implements Standard JSON Schema, which sets the type and can carry a default:

```ts
export default defineNuxtConfig({
  runtimeConfig: {
    apiSecret: z.string(), // required, must be set at runtime
    port: 3000, // NUXT_PORT=abc fails
    session: z.object({
      secure: z.stringbool().default(true),
      maxAge: z.number().int().optional(),
    }),
    public: {
      mode: z.enum(['preview', 'production']).default('preview'),
    },
  },
})
```

